quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  2,238,"Be (constantly) watchful of your prayers, and (especially) the middle prayer, and stand before Allah with all devotion."
  2,239,"When you fear (danger), pray on foot or while riding, and when you are safe again, remember Allah, as He has taught you what you did not know."
  2,240,"Those of you who (are about to) die leaving widows behind shall bequeath for their wives, providing (them) a year’s maintenance without causing them to leave their homes. However, if they leave (of their own accord), you are not accountable for what they decide for themselves according to reasonable norms. And Allah is All-Mighty, All-Wise."
  2,241,"For divorced women, there shall (also) be a provision according to honourable norms. (This is) an obligation on the God-conscious."
  2,242,Thus does Allah clarify His revelations to you so that you may understand (the laws and norms).
  2,243,"Have you not seen those who left their homelands fearing death, and they were in thousands? Allah said to them: ‘Die’ (and they died). Then He revived them. Indeed, Allah is Gracious to humankind, but most people are not grateful."
  2,244,"So fight in the way of Allah, and know that Allah is All-Hearing, All-Knowing."
  2,245,"Who shall lend Allah a generous loan which He may multiply for him manifold? And Allah seizes and expands (the means of life), and to Him shall you be returned."
